IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] (פקודת מס הכנסה [נוסח חדש]), s 66(c)(4)-(6) before 2024.
-- THE NOUNS OF PART A: DECLARE and nothing else.
-- (Part B, s 121B in tax year 2025, uses the nouns of row IL-03, vendored beside this file
-- as ito-il03-nouns.l4, byte for byte; see NOTES.md section 8.)
--
-- Sources: the enacting Acts, deposited as PDFs under
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/
-- (24_lsr_624898.pdf = Sefer HaChukim 2972, 18 May 2022; 25_lsr_2656507.pdf = SH 3048,
-- 7 June 2023; 25_lsr_4239836.pdf = SH 3184, 20 March 2024), and the Hebrew Wikisource
-- consolidation of the Ordinance, raw wikitext, sha256 b87f2cf4...b81b6, quoted by line.
-- The Acts' text layers scramble digits and parentheses, so every figure here was read from
-- the page image and then checked against the text layer (NOTES.md section 7).
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or a register or a return records it.
-- Whether the fact earns a credit point is a rule, and belongs in the rules module.

§ `Nouns for section 66(c)(4)-(6) before 2024`

§§ `The claimant`

-- Section 66(c) gives the credit points for a child to one of four people, by paragraph.
-- Which of the four a taxpayer is, is the caller's classification (IL-02 decides who is the
-- woman and who the man of a couple); it is recorded on the return and the marriage register.
-- src:2465 | (4) האשה תהא זכאית ל־ 1 ⁄ 2 נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36א, ובנוסף וכנגד המס החל על הכנסתה מיגיעה אישית – לנקודות זיכוי בעד ילדיה כלהלן:
-- src:2472 | (4א) בחישוב המס של אישה שנישאה לאלמן יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי בעד כל אחד מילדיו, כאמור בפסקה (4);
-- src:2473 | (5) הגבר יהא זכאי, כנגד המס החל על הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית, לנקודות זיכוי בעד כל אחד מילדיו, כלהלן:
-- src:2478 | (6) בחישוב המס של גבר שנישא לאלמנה יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי בעד כל אחד מילדיה, כאמור בפסקה (5).
DECLARE `A claimant under section 66(c)(4)-(6)` IS ONE OF
    `a woman, under paragraph (4)`
    `a woman who married a widower, under paragraph (4A)`
    `a man, under paragraph (5)`
    `a man who married a widow, under paragraph (6)`

§§ `The child`

-- One child, as the return records them.
-- The age bands of s 66(c)(4) and (5) are counted in tax years, from the year of birth:
-- src:1644 | ”שנת לידה“ – שנת המס שבה נולד הילד;
-- src:1645 | ”שנת בגרות“ – שנת המס שבה מלאו לילד שמונה עשרה שנים.
DECLARE `A child in section 66(c)` HAS
    `tax year of birth` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The vintages of section 66(c)(4)-(6)`

-- The text of paragraphs (4), (5) and (6) that governs the income of a tax year.
-- This names the vintage; it does not hold its words. Only the first is held (by the Acts).
DECLARE `A vintage of section 66(c)(4)-(6)` IS ONE OF
    `the text of Acts SH 3048 and SH 3184, from tax year 2024`
    `the base text with the temporary provision of Act SH 2972, in tax year 2022`
    `the base text, in tax year 2023`
    `a text before tax year 2022`

§§ `The reading of Act SH 2972 on the age limit`

-- Act SH 2972 gives a further credit point for a child who in 2022 had not yet completed thirteen
-- years (its words are quoted in il31-ito66-vintages.l4). The text does not say on which day
-- of 2022 the age is tested, and the readings give different answers for a child born in 2009.
-- Where the text is silent and the readings part, the reading is a switch: ruled by Meng on
-- 2026-10-08 (SHRUG), one named switch, declined by default, every other reading kept by name.
-- A reading is an argument of a rule, never a field of a record.
DECLARE `A reading of Act SH 2972 on the age limit of thirteen years in 2022` IS ONE OF
    `the age is counted in tax years, so a child born in 2009 has completed thirteen years in 2022`
    `the age is tested at the start of 2022, so a child born in 2009 has not completed thirteen years`
    `declined where the reading changes the answer`  -- the default
